 LUMEN Project Rules — Trae IDE

## Identity
You are building LUMEN: a self-hosted AI research agent (Manus + OpenClaw alternative).
Stack: Python 3.11, FastAPI, LangGraph, OpenRouter, Tavily, Firecrawl, Telegram Bot API.

## Code Style
- Use async/await throughout — never sync blocking calls
- All configs in .env — never hardcode API keys
- Type hints on every function
- Max 80 chars per line
- Docstring on every class and public function

## File Structure (enforce strictly)
lumen/
  main.py              # FastAPI entry
  agent/               # loop, planner, searcher, scraper, synthesiser
  skills/              # SKILL.md plugin system
  memory/              # Markdown on-disk manager
  telegram/            # Bot handlers
  config.py            # Pydantic settings from .env
  requirements.txt

## API Provider
- Primary: OpenRouter (base_url: https://openrouter.ai/api/v1)
- Default model: anthropic/claude-sonnet-4-6
- Fallback model: deepseek/deepseek-chat
- Always pass HTTP-Referer and X-Title headers to OpenRouter

## Output Rules
- Show me the file path before writing each file
- Ask for confirmation before deleting any file
- After each phase, run: pip install -r requirements.txt
- Write tests for every agent module in /tests
